eMutability\":\"pure\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{\"seedFaceUnits()\":{\"details\":\"A single-token exit of more than ~30% of the pool trips Balancer's minimum invariant ratio\"}},\"details\":\"Face token. `BalancerV3PoolStandardExchangeTarget.getTokensIn()` excludes the virtual buffer\\n *      token (`ttaToken()` / `bufferToken()` / `bufferToken(i)`), so the buffer token (DAI) is not a\\n *      valid `tokenIn` for `tokenOut == pool` and `previewExchangeIn(dai, x, pool)` reverts\\n *      `InvalidRoute`. The face is therefore the leg-0 Aerodrome SE share, which is a physical pool\\n *      token, 18 decimals (Aerodrome SE shares keep the LP decimals with offset 0), and a member of\\n *      the pool's `vaultTokens()`.\\n *\\n *      Deployment order (M10 / section 11). The harness runs the family TestBase `setUp` inside this\\n *      fixture's constructor, i.e. inside the hook test's `setUp`, with no Vault or PoolManager lock\\n *      held: Vault + router, nested IndexedEx manager, Aerodrome SE legs, rate provider, package,\\n *      pool, `router.initialize`. Only after that does the hook TestBase deploy the hook.\\n *\\n *      Handles. The harness is a `new`-deployed TestBase, so `InitDevService.initEnv(address(this))`\\n *      gives it its own CREATE3 factory and IndexedEx manager (the shared factory's `deployFacet` is\\n *      `onlyOwnerOrOperator`, and the hook test contract owns it). `Ctx.owner` equals the harness\\n *      owner (`makeAddr(\\\"owner\\\")`). The single-CP package validates the SE by arguments and decimals,\\n *      not by registry membership (`_validateArgs`), so a pool registered on the harness manager binds.\\n *\\n *      R14. No partial case: the native BPT route takes exactly the input or reverts\\n *      (`PoolLiquidityFundingMismatch`), and `pretransferred = true` is rejected\\n *      (`UnsupportedPoolPretransfer`); the hook uses the pull route. `seBooked()` is 0 because the\\n *      pool keeps no face-token book; the buffer-token view is exposed as `bufferBooked()`.\\n *\\n *      Operative failure. `armOperativeRevert` mocks two pool dependencies, never the pool, hook,\\n *      package or registry: the leg-0 Aerodrome SE `exchangeIn` (the fold the pool hooks perform on\\n *      buffer reconciliation) and the Balancer VaultMock `addLiquidity` / `removeLiquidity` (the\\n *      calls `executePoolLiquidity` makes inside `Vault.unlock`). `Vault.unlock` uses\\n *      `Address.functionCall`, which bubbles the callback revert bytes unchanged, so the pool and\\n *      then the hook revert with `rejectBytes()`. Previews touch neither selector.\\n \",\"errors\":{\"DependencyRejected(bytes32)\":[{\"details\":\"Non-SUT dependency failure payload used by `armOperativeRevert` implementations.\"}]},\"stateVariables\":{\"SHARE_TREASURY\":{\"details\":\"Holds minted leg shares so `fund` can hand out exact raw amounts.\"}},\"title\":\"SeMatrix_BalancerBufferPoolFixtureBase\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"legStandardExchange()\":{\"notice\":\"Leg-0 Aerodrome SE (a dependency of the pool, not the SUT); equals `faceToken()`.\"},\"bufferToken()\":{\"notice\":\"Leg-0 buffer token (DAI). Virtual on the native BPT route; not the face.\"},\"bufferBooked()\":{\"notice\":\"Pool booked buffer view (`virtualTTA()` / `virtualBuffer()`), Vault scaled18.\"},\"fund(address,uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Give `to` exactly `amount` raw leg-0 SE shares, minted through the real Aerodrome         LP -> SE deposit path into a treasury and then transferred.\"},\"seBooked()\":{\"notice\":\"0: the pool keeps no face-token book. See `bufferBooked()` for the buffer view.\"},\"seedFaceUnits()\":{\"notice\":\"      (`InvariantRatioBelowMin(0, 0.7e18)` on the hook's full-claim valuation); keep the hook small.\"},\"partialDeploymentBalance()\":{\"notice\":\"Independent protocol custody measurement for fixtures whose requested allowance cannot express exact consumption. Values are denominated in native face-token units.\"},\"sweepsOnNextInvest()\":{\"notice\":\"True when a later investing operation sweeps the booked remainder (D31). False for         families whose face input is a permanent sleeve credit on the buffering route         (Lido: WETH→SE credits `liquidReserveEth`; only `rebalance` / `exchangeInEth` stake).\"},\"operativeRevertReachable()\":{\"notice\":\"True when the hook's buffering route reaches an operative dependency call that         `armOperativeRevert` can make fail. False when the route only books locally (Lido).\"}},\"notice\":\"Shared body of the six Balancer V3 buffer-pool SE fixtures (WP6). The SE is the pool\\n *         diamond itself: its own BPT is the SE share (D38) and its native Standard Exchange route\\n *         (`BalancerV3PoolStandardExchangeTarget`) joins and exits through the real Vault\\n *         `addLiquidity` / `removeLiquidity`.\\n *\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"test/foundry/spec/hooks/uniswap/v4/standardExchange/SeMatrix_BalancerBufferPoolFixtureBase.sol\":\"SeMatrix_BalancerBufferPoolFixtureBase\"},\"evmVersion\":\"osaka\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":1},\"remappings\":[\"@battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/src/\",\"@crane/=lib/crane/\",\"@matterlabs/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/lib/\",\"@nomicfoundation/=node_modules/@nomicfoundation/\",\"@opengsn/=node_modules/@opengsn/\",\"@openzeppelin/=node_modules/@openzeppelin/\",\"@oz/=lib/crane/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\"@ozu/=lib/crane/contracts/external/openzeppelin-upgradeable/\",\"battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/\",\"battlechain-lib-mocks/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/test/mocks/\",\"battlechain-lib/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/src/\",\"battlechain-s